      }},
      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The influence of D,L-alpha-tocopherol (vitamin E) on the plasma total and very low-density lipoprotein, low density lipoprotein, and high-density lipoprotein cholesterol and triglyceride was studied in one normolipidemic and four hypertriglyceridemic subjects. Overall vitamin E caused no decrease in plasma total, very low-density and low-density lipoprotein cholesterol and triglyceride concentrations and no increase in high-density lipoprotein cholesterol level. D,L-alpha-Tocopherol does not seem to have any consistent effect on plasma lipids and lipoproteins in these patients."},
